  "question": {
    "text": "For a real number <math><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo></math> if the system <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>&#945;</mi></mtd><mtd><msup><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>&#945;</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>&#945;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mi>&#945;</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>z</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced></math> of linear equations, has infinitely many solutions, then <math><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Determinant value of 3<math><mo>×</mo> </math>3 matrix should be zero for infinite solution</p><p><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>α</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>±</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>But at &nbsp;<math><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, three equations become parallel, so no solution so rejected</p><p>at &nbsp; <math><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, All three equation become</p><p><math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp; (coincident planes), so infinite solution.</p><p><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
